BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-unil-micro-seminar-2026-12-08-toan-le-2026-12-08@tracker
SUMMARY:UNIL Micro Seminar: Toan Lê
DTSTAMP:20261116T171026Z
DTSTART:20261208T110000
DTEND:20261208T121500
DESCRIPTION:Seminar in Microeconomics\, UNIL (Faculty of Business and Econo
	mics\, HEC Lausanne)\nPresenter: Toan Lê (University of Helsinki)\nTitle: 
	Strategy Proofness versus Collusion Proofness\nOrganizer: Prof. Bettina Kl
	aus\nFormat: on site + online\n\nAbstract: How welfare is shared shapes in
	dividual and collective incentives. Connects efficient mechanism design to
	 the cooperative theory of value\; a Reduction Principle characterises fea
	sible combinations of individual and coalition incentives through ownershi
	p constraints on Harsanyi welfare dividends. Also yields an ownership cond
	ition for bribery-proofness\, and compares first- vs second-price auctions
	 on individual incentives vs cartel regret.
LOCATION:UNIL Extranef\, Room 109\, Lausanne
CATEGORIES:Tracker,Event
END:VEVENT
